    "ref": "PR #915 (fix); fix evidence: 01/10/2026: on a local stand a Joomla site born while TRACY_ORIGIN was http://tracy.test:8080 (before f3367844b2, 11/09) kept `$live_site = 'http://tracy-ai-8836f920.tracy.test:8080'`; pages rendered, but signing in or out inside the Browser tab showed 'tracy-ai-8836f920.tracy.test refused to connect'. Reproduced 05/10 on vincent-testing1 with live_site set to :8080: GET /index.php?option=com_users&view=login answered 301 to :8080 and the Browser tab showed the same error; after the fix the same GET and a sign-in POST (303) stay on :51710.",
    "invariant": "S2 exits 0 with 0 failures, 0 skipped, 0 cancelled. \"a redirect to the site's OWN hostname on a stale port or scheme lands on the address the visitor used\" passes: a site answering `Location: http://stale.tracy.test:8080/` or `https://stale.tracy.test/en/?x=1` to a visitor on `http://stale.tracy.test:51710` is reframed to `http://stale.tracy.test:51710/` and `http://stale.tracy.test:51710/en/?x=1`. 'a redirect to a THIRD party is left exactly as the site wrote it' still passes: `https://checkout.stripe.com/x` is not touched. 'a redirect naming the INTERNAL container is reframed onto the address the visitor used', both EmDash redirect tests and 'a local CMS redirect that adds a port to its Docker hostname stays on the public site' still pass. S4: Changing origin A to B at arbitrary ports updates managed policy exactly once on WordPress, Joomla and EmDash; content/mail/publish survive, custom and none remain unchanged, invalid or unsigned calls cannot write, and failed reconciliation returns a framable message before upstream.",
